1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,960
Range sets how much sound path the Epoch shows across the screen, from the left edge to the right edge.

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:14,580
The Epoch is already calibrated for the steel step block. First, drag the probe onto the 0.500 inch step.

3
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:20,540
On the screen, the initial pulse is on the left, and the first back-wall echo is in the middle.

4
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:30,180
Press F1 for the Basic menu, then P3 to select Range. Each click of the knob now changes the range by 0.01 inch.

5
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:35,810
Turn the knob down to 0.700 inch. You can hold the knob down to turn faster.

6
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:39,120
How many back-wall echoes do you see? Just one.

7
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:47,680
Back-wall echoes from the 0.500 inch step come every half inch: at 0.5, 1.0, 1.5 inches, and so on.

8
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:55,970
The screen now ends at 0.700. The echo at 0.5 fits. The next one, at 1.0, is past the right edge.

9
00:00:55,970 --> 00:01:02,790
Turn up to 1.100 inches. Now the echoes at 0.5 and 1.0 both fit. Two echoes.

10
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:07,660
Now guess before you turn. At 1.600 inches, how many will fit?

11
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:15,400
The echoes at 0.5, 1.0 and 1.5 are all inside 1.6, so three. Turn the knob and check.

12
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:20,890
Three. At 3.100 inches, the echoes up to 3.0 fit: six of them.

13
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:28,300
And at 5.100 inches, ten. The last ones are small, because every trip through the steel loses a little energy.

14
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:38,820
One more thing to watch. Look at the G1 thickness box at the top of the screen. Gate 1 is on the first back-wall echo, and it reads 0.500 inch.

15
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:44,270
Keep your eye on it while we change the range. Down to 2.500 inches.

16
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:47,420
Down to 0.700.

17
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:50,570
And up to 4.000.

18
00:01:50,570 --> 00:02:00,060
The echoes slid across the screen, but the reading stayed 0.500 every time. The back wall is still 0.500 inch below the probe.

19
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:03,440
Range changes what you see, not what you measure.

20
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:13,770
A small range spreads one echo out so you can see it clearly. A large range shows several back-wall echoes, which you need for a two-back-wall calibration.

21
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:17,760
Now try it yourself on the Epoch below.
